rr software ticks (rr's tracee ABI version 1) on the loops of glibc's x86-64 assembly.

Every cycle in the code of every function assembled from x86-64 assembly source (the string,
memory and wide-character functions of every ISA level, __mpn_*, the spin lock, libm's x87
functions, libmvec's vector math: in libc.so.6, ld.so, libm.so.6, libmvec.so.1 and the
static archives) gets an RR_SOFTTICK (glibc-101) on each way round.  A tick goes on a line of
its own before the first instruction of a source line (after the labels that start it), where
no arithmetic flag is live in any object that assembles that line, since it clobbers them;
where possible in a block that every cycle of the loop passes, so that one tick per iteration
cuts them all.  A tick in a shared template (memmove-vec-unaligned-erms.S, strcmp-avx2.S,
...) is in every variant that includes it.

The places were chosen from the machine code of a build with glibc-101 (its control-flow
graph, the jump tables, the flags' liveness, and gas's DWARF line table back to the source);
softticks/ticks-2.41.json lists each tick, where it is assembled, and which loop it cuts.
Without __RR_SOFTTICKS__ RR_SOFTTICK is empty: the object code is the same.

diff --git a/sysdeps/x86_64/addmul_1.S b/sysdeps/x86_64/addmul_1.S
--- a/sysdeps/x86_64/addmul_1.S
+++ b/sysdeps/x86_64/addmul_1.S
@@ -72,7 +72,9 @@ L(odd):	add	$1, %rbx
 	jmp	L(e)
 
 	.p2align 4
-L(top):	mul	%rcx
+L(top):
+	RR_SOFTTICK
+	mul	%rcx
 	ADDSUB	%r8, %r10
 	lea	(%rax), %r8
 	mov	(up,%rbx,8), %rax
diff --git a/sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/e_fmodl.S b/sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/e_fmodl.S
--- a/sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/e_fmodl.S
+++ b/sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/e_fmodl.S
@@ -11,7 +11,9 @@ RCSID("$NetBSD: $")
 ENTRY(__ieee754_fmodl)
